  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Radioactive nuclide X decays into a stable nuclide Y. The decay constant of X is λ. The variation with time t of number of nuclei of X and Y are shown on the same axes.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the expression for s?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\textit{ln 2}}{\\lambda}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{\\lambda}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda}{\\textit{ln 2}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"ln 2\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
